<entry>
  <id>blog/20220823-privateeye-314.html</id>
  <author><name>David Thomas</name></author>
  <title type="html">PrivateEye 3.14</title>
  <published>2022-08-23T00:00:00Z</published>
  
  <category term="Blog"></category>
  
  <category term="RISC OS"></category>
  
  <category term="PrivateEye"></category>
  
  <link href="http://www.davespace.co.uk/blog/20220823-privateeye-314.html" rel="alternate"></link>
  <content type="html"><![CDATA[
    
    
    
<p><a href="/risc.os/privateeye.html">PrivateEye</a> 3.14 is now available.</p>
<p><a href="/software/eyesnap6.png"><img src="/software/thumbs/eyesnap6.png" alt="Peter Default" /></a></p>
<p>PrivateEye is a viewer for Sprites, DrawFiles, JPEGs, ArtWorks, GIFs and PNGs. It also has editing features including bitmap effects and rotation.</p>
<p>Version 3.14 is a minor update with a selection of tweaks and bug fixes:</p>
<ul>
<li>When loading new images the &ldquo;Fit to screen&rdquo; mode will now only ever scale downwards. This is more helpful than the previous behaviour which would scale small images up to needlessly enormous proportions. Note that the &ldquo;Fit screen&rdquo; button on the scale view dialogue is unaffected.</li>
<li>The data transfer system has had an upgrade:
<ul>
<li>An app-to-app transfer won&rsquo;t result in <code>&lt;Wimp$Scrap&gt;</code> used in title bars now. It&rsquo;ll use <code>&lt;untitled&gt;</code> in title bars, and <code>ImageFile</code> when saving an image with no known name. Received files are marked as modified too. This matches the behaviour of standard RISC OS apps.</li>
<li>Message_DataOpen template mode (when <code>est_size</code> is -2) is supported (it&rsquo;s not super useful because PrivateEye&rsquo;s not a full editor, but it is in there).</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li>libpng has been upgraded to 1.6.37.</li>
</ul>

    
    
  ]]></content>
</entry>



